# Caches only, at any depth. .clj-kondo/imports holds the linter configs that
# libraries export (Promesa's p/loop and p/let among them), and without them a
# fresh clone fails bb check with five bogus "Unresolved symbol" errors. They
# are 32K across 8 files against an 18M cache, so the configs are tracked and
# the caches are not.
#
# The ** matters. An anchored ".clj-kondo/.cache" only covers the root, which
# would start tracking example caches, and those embed absolute paths from
# whoever last ran the linter.
**/.clj-kondo/.cache

# The examples' own .clj-kondo is ignored outright. Its imports are stale
# debris from an unrelated checkout (next.jdbc, hiccup, aero, none of which
# any example uses), and bb check lints from the root config anyway.
example/*/.clj-kondo
.lsp
# clojure-mcp
.clojure-mcp/
mcp-toolkit.jar
